---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
	title="About Steven Yule, chartered civil engineer"
	sheet="About"
	description="Steven Yule, chartered civil engineer in Dubai, with 17 years making digital and AI useful on live capital programmes across the GCC and the UK."
>
	<div class="page-head">
		<div class="kicker">Who I am</div>
		<h1 class="page-title">About Steven Yule</h1>
		<p class="lede">
			A chartered civil engineer who thinks in systems, across the whole life
			of what gets built.
		</p>
	</div>
	<h2 class="section-title">From an asset to a city</h2>
	<div class="career">
		<div class="career-step">
			<div class="career-art">
				<img
					src="/drawings/career-bridge-475.webp"
					srcset="/drawings/career-bridge-475.webp 475w, /drawings/career-bridge-950.webp 950w"
					sizes="16rem"
					width="475"
					height="225"
					decoding="async"
					alt=""
				/>
			</div>
			<div class="career-year">2009</div>
			<div class="career-place">Birmingham</div>
			<div class="career-text">Bridge rehabilitation on a maintenance contract. It taught me that every design decision has whole-life consequences.</div>
			<div class="career-shock"><span>2009 financial crisis</span></div>
		</div>
		<div class="career-step">
			<div class="career-art">
				<img
					src="/drawings/career-network-580.webp"
					srcset="/drawings/career-network-580.webp 580w, /drawings/career-network-1160.webp 1160w"
					sizes="16rem"
					width="580"
					height="368"
					decoding="async"
					alt=""
				/>
			</div>
			<div class="career-year">2012</div>
			<div class="career-place">Doha</div>
			<div class="career-text">Operations and asset management, then setting up a new branch. This is where I learned the business.</div>
			<div class="career-shock"><span>2014 oil price fall</span></div>
		</div>
		<div class="career-step">
			<div class="career-art">
				<img
					src="/drawings/career-portfolio-720.webp"
					srcset="/drawings/career-portfolio-720.webp 720w, /drawings/career-portfolio-1440.webp 1440w"
					sizes="16rem"
					width="720"
					height="380"
					decoding="async"
					alt=""
				/>
			</div>
			<div class="career-year">2017</div>
			<div class="career-place">The UK</div>
			<div class="career-text">A major rail programme, then an asset management practice and operations across consulting and digital.</div>
			<div class="career-shock"><span>2020 COVID</span></div>
		</div>
		<div class="career-step now">
			<div class="career-art">
				<img
					src="/drawings/career-city-840.webp"
					srcset="/drawings/career-city-840.webp 840w, /drawings/career-city-1680.webp 1680w"
					sizes="16rem"
					width="840"
					height="380"
					decoding="async"
					alt=""
				/>
			</div>
			<div class="career-year">2022</div>
			<div class="career-place">Dubai and Riyadh</div>
			<div class="career-text">I chose to build a digital and data practice from a standing start and led the first integrated infrastructure plan for Riyadh.</div>
			<div class="career-shock"><span>2026 conflict</span></div>
		</div>
	</div>
	<div class="band band-blue">
		<p>
			<strong>In each downturn the money moved to different work.</strong> Each
			time I built something new from where it went. An owner whose plans
			change faces the same question, which is what can move to keep the
			portfolio in range.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div class="prose">
		<picture class="about-photo">
			<source
				type="image/webp"
				srcset="/steven-yule-portrait-360.webp 360w, /steven-yule-portrait-720.webp 720w"
				sizes="(min-width: 40em) 13rem, 9rem"
			/>
			<img
				class="portrait"
				src="/steven-yule-portrait-360.jpg"
				srcset="/steven-yule-portrait-360.jpg 360w, /steven-yule-portrait-720.jpg 720w"
				sizes="(min-width: 40em) 13rem, 9rem"
				alt="Steven Yule"
				width="360"
				height="450"
			/>
		</picture>
		<p>
			I lead digital, data and AI work for infrastructure at director level,
			based in Dubai. For 17 years I have worked in the Gulf and the UK on
			making technology useful once it meets a live capital programme.
		</p>
		<p>
			I have built and led teams in digital strategy, data engineering, data
			science and software delivery. I also ran a regional digital and data
			practice. That meant answering for its growth as well as the quality of
			its work. Running a practice taught me to judge a digital idea on two
			counts. Will it work on a real asset? Can the organisation buy it and
			afford to run it for years? The second question is usually the harder
			one.
		</p>
		<p>
			Most digital capability stalls in the same place. It is proven in a
			pilot and treated as finished because it worked once. The real test is
			whether a live programme can depend on it. I spend most of my time on
			that gap. It is usually settled
			earlier than people expect, in the procurement and in who owns what at
			handover. Large owners meet the same gap at portfolio level. Each
			development can be relied on alone while the portfolio as a whole misses
			its range.
		</p>
		<div class="case wide">
			<figure class="drawing case-drawing">
				<img
					src="/drawings/cover-city-720.webp"
					srcset="/drawings/cover-city-720.webp 720w, /drawings/cover-city-1440.webp 1440w"
					sizes="(min-width: 62em) 24rem, 100vw"
					width="720"
					height="561"
					loading="lazy"
					decoding="async"
					alt="Line drawing of a city district raised above its utility layer, with one service corridor marked in red."
				/>
			</figure>
			<div class="case-body">
				<div class="case-client">Riyadh Infrastructure Projects Center (RIPC)</div>
				<div class="case-figure">More than 5,000 conflicts prevented</div>
				<p class="case-context">
					The first integrated infrastructure plan for the Riyadh region, with
					me as project director.
				</p>
				<dl class="case-rows">
					<div class="case-row">
						<dt>Before</dt>
						<dd>Road space and working time were contested site by site.</dd>
					</div>
					<div class="case-row">
						<dt>The plan</dt>
						<dd>
							The works programmes of more than 20 government and utility bodies in
							one plan covering thousands of projects.
						</dd>
					</div>
					<div class="case-row">
						<dt>The result</dt>
						<dd>
							Road space and working time could be booked once, by agreement. The
							plan is publicly credited with preventing more than 5,000 conflicts
							between their works.
						</dd>
					</div>
				</dl>
			</div>
		</div>
		<p>
			The work is commissioned in three ways. An <a href="/review/"
				>independent review</a
			> gives an owner a written opinion on a decision before it is confirmed.
			Continuing advisory covers decisions that keep arriving over months. A
			non-executive or board appointment is for challenge that has to happen
			in the boardroom. A review is the simplest place to start. All three are
			described under <a href="/work/">Work</a>.
		</p>
		<p>
			My background covers transport, utilities, smart cities and the built
			environment. It also covers data-centre enablement and asset-heavy
			capital programmes in the UK and the Gulf.
		</p>
		<p>
			I am a Fellow of the Institution of Civil Engineers (CEng FICE), an ICE
			Policy Fellow and the ICE UAE Country Representative. I am also a Fellow
			of the Chartered Institution of Highways and Transportation (FCIHT) and
			a member of the Institute of Asset Management (MIAM). I am a Freeman of
			the Worshipful Company of Engineers and a non-executive director of
			Thomas Telford Ltd.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div class="origin-note">
		<h2 class="origin-note-title">About the name</h2>
		<p>
			OkArthur is named after my son Arthur, who is seven and asks more
			questions, and sharper ones, than I am always ready for. Ok, Arthur
			became the answer, and then it became the name. Taking a question
			seriously, and not settling for the defensible answer, is most of what
			good advice turns out to be.
		</p>
	</div>
</Base>
